body:
@user I built a prod bundle and profiled it.

Root cause: toggling a checkbox re-renders the avatar subtree (`ReportActionAvatars` + its per-row `useOnyx(REPORT)`) for **every** visible row, not just the tapped one — the page rebuilds its option objects each toggle, so every row's `item` is a new ref and React Compiler can't bail on identity. Extracting the avatar into a child keyed on primitives (`reportID`/`accountID`/`policyID`) lets the compiler bail it — verified in prod, **17 → 0** avatar re-renders per toggle, zero regressioon.

but i'll be straigth: on my repro (15 rows, seeded contacts, idle machine) the whole toggle is already ~12 ms, so this doesn't move INP — and a `useDeferredValue` variant didn't either. It's the "insufficient data" case; my synthetic list isn't slow enough to reproduce the real thing.

@user What solution do you propose? Add code diffs.

Also, please describe in detail what I need to test to determine whether this is a front-end or back-end error (specifically, which values I should check and where).

If possible, please also find the PR where this logic was originally added.
